/context-switching-the-security-function/","https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-docs/concepts/other-timeframes-and-data/#lower-timeframe-data","https://www.tradingview.com/support/solutions/43000502018-volume-weighted-average-price-vwap/","https://www.tradingview.com/pine-script-docs/language/type-system/#float","https://github.com/binance/binance-public-data"],"method":{"165":["The saved chart is Binance Futures BTC_USDT 1d. The active trend filter requests its own market at 60 minutes and calculates SMA(20) in hourly context. Pine v2 defaults to legacy lookahead_on, which selects the first hourly bar on completed historical dates. Its close and SMA are already known 23 hours before the next daily order fill. The comparator does not claim realtime parity because realtime lower-timeframe request selection differs.","Both Pine backends and an independent implementation agree on every first-hour close and hourly SMA, 20-day basis and population deviation, authored 4×/2×/8× band rules, strict direction gates, four eligible order instructions, and next-open one-way positions and fills. The old eager calculations are evaluated before their conditions.","The archive does not pin a broker lot size or fee. The comparison uses one unit of base asset, 10,000 USDT accounting base and 0.059% commission per fill. No original wallet state is assumed."],"5599":["The source uses vwap(close) on the explicit native 1d cryptocurrency chart, so session VWAP resets every single bar. It equals the only daily close observation to Pine's nine fractional comparison digits. Both the entry and add predicates require close strictly above this value.","Both Pine backends and the independent single-weight arithmetic match all 1,484 verified observations. The conditional Bollinger take-profit close is allowed to occur while flat and generates no order. The unused legacy dates, session helper and commented stop are outside the active order path.","Source capital and quantity are retained. The 